{
 "_source": {
  "how": "docker run --rm --network none IMAGE sh -c 'SETUP CASE; echo \"rc=$?\"', one run per case; SETUP writes the files f, p, empty and blank and the folder d in /tmp and changes to it",
  "setup": "printf 'root:x:0:0\\ndaemon:x:1:1\\n\"root\" said\\na/b c\\nnobody:x:65534\\n' > /tmp/f; printf 'root\\ndaemon\\n' > /tmp/p; : > /tmp/empty; printf 'nobody\\n\\n' > /tmp/blank; mkdir /tmp/d; cd /tmp; ",
  "date": "2026-10-22",
  "what": "grep -e and -f take the patterns, a double quote and a slash stay in the pattern; the BusyBox images' case `grep -f d f` (a folder given to -f, rc 1, no text) is recorded but not asserted: test_patch.py skips it (gnu_only), because the persona's grep has GNU's texts and BusyBox reads a folder given to -f as an empty file (inferred from rc 1 and no text, not asserted)"
 },
